{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792449396,"nonce":"nzrBL2peVx2QzJO5zpKfQ8QBfxc=","message":"4683ac3b49bdd4db94730514d65afe71dcf693f0 on main fixes expanded Git history failing to reopen after a bulk close action.\n\nClose Others, Close Saved and Close All previously only replaced Workbench.open. They bypassed closeFile, so Studio.closeTab never notified the embedded VM to unmount the history root. The script's opened guard and native history cursor remained alive even after the visible tab disappeared. All three actions now use closeFile for every removed tab, retaining the existing active-tab and unsaved-buffer behavior.\n\nRegression evidence: before the change, the UI-driven Git snapshot failed with \"timed out waiting for Close others to unmount history\" (bin/git-reopen-before.log). With the fix, the complete Git scenario passes in dark and light, including actual tab-X close/reopen, repeated sidebar-maximize cycles, every bulk close menu followed by sidebar maximize, graph hook cleanup, virtual scrolling and fiber recovery. Basic and Documents scenarios also pass in both schemes, including retained undo for closed unsaved documents and eviction of closed saved caches. git diff --check passes.\n\nInspected the reopened graph previews in both schemes under bin/git-reopen-snapshots/rayde-{dark,light}-git-history-reopened-after-close-all.png. Native executable and macOS app bundle rebuilt. No sibling source changes, extra worktrees or new Cargo target directories. No pushes. Keep the Git umbrella issue open for its remaining features.","files":null}]}